#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A bare and cold concrete floor."
msgstr "むき出しの冷えたコンクリート床です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blue floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A blue section of flooring."
msgstr "青色の床です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A dirt grave, with some grass growing on it.  At least some of the dead do "
"actually rest in peace."
msgstr "少し草が茂った、既に埋まっている墓穴です。少なくともここにいる死者は安らかに眠っています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down."
msgstr "目の細かい土を押し固めて作った床です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "stone masonry floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A floor of carefully cut and laid stones, joined with mortar."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A fresh grave, covered with stones, either to keep something from digging it"
" up or to keep one inside from digging out of it.  Or both.  Two planks mark"
" this place of someone's eternal rest."
msgstr ""
"真新しい墓穴です。誰かが掘り返さないように、あるいは中からこじ開けられないように、石の蓋が置いてあります。2枚の板切れは、ここが誰かに永遠の寝床を提供する場所であることを示す印です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of upturned dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A giant hill of dirt that looks like you could crawl inside for shelter."
msgstr "大きな土の山です。中を掘りぬけばシェルターになりそうです。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "green floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A green section of flooring."
msgstr "緑色の床です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rubber mulch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area mulched with shredded rubber.  It's a softer place to land than"
" regular dirt."
msgstr "細かく砕いたゴムを敷き詰めた広い床です。通常の地面より着地の衝撃を吸収しやすい構造になっています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "orifice"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large round orifice, with trails of fresh and dried-up strange green "
"liquid with a strongly acidic odor covering its inner sides."
msgstr "大きな丸い開口部の内側には、まだ乾ききっていない緑色の液体が残っており、酸の臭いを発しています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A metal gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but "
"not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr "狭い隙間に渡して使う、金属製の通路です。床の役割は十分に果たせる強度ですが、追加の床材を支えられるほど頑丈ではありません。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A mound of sand."
msgstr "砂の山です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles."
msgstr "より美しく霜が付きにくい表面仕上げが施された、比較的新しい公共区画のコンクリートです。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles.  Covered with a streak of yellow paint."
msgstr "より美しく霜が付きにくい表面仕上げが施された、比較的新しい公共区画のコンクリートです。黄色の塗料で縞模様が描かれています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "glassed sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A patch of sand with a crust of natural glass atop it from exposure to "
"intense heat."
msgstr "表面の砂が極度の高温に晒され、天然のガラス層になっています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "red floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A red section of flooring."
msgstr "赤色の床です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rock floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A relatively flat area of rock and stone.  Looks stable enough to be mined "
"with the proper mining gear."
msgstr "比較的平坦な岩石の床です。安定しており、適切な道具があれば掘削できそうです。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "linoleum tile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A section of flooring made out of a tough, gray, rubbery material."
msgstr "ゴムのような丈夫な素材で作られた、灰色の床です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "linoleum tile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, rubbery material.  Colored a "
"simple white."
msgstr "ゴムのような丈夫な素材で作られた、シンプルな白色の床です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A segment of asphalt, slowly degrading from cracks, frost heaves, and lack "
"of maintenance."
msgstr "アスファルトの一部は氷結や整備不足からゆっくりとひび割れ、劣化し始めています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull coating, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix.  Used "
"for runways, and can't be melted by jet engine nozzles."
msgstr "軍用のエポキシ樹脂で覆われた厚い金属製の甲板表面です。滑走路として使われ、ジェットエンジンのノズルから噴出される熱でも溶かせません。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "white deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix and "
"painted white."
msgstr "白線が引いてある、軍用のエポキシ樹脂で覆われた厚い金属製の甲板表面です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix and "
"painted yellow."
msgstr "黄色の線が引いてある、軍用のエポキシ樹脂で覆われた厚い金属製の甲板表面です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "red deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix, and "
"painted red."
msgstr "赤色の線が引いてある、軍用のエポキシ樹脂で覆われた厚い金属製の甲板表面です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "paper thin slag"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thin splatter of slag coats the ground here, having cooled completely into"
" something like pitted stone."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal grate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A walkway that can be used as a protective covering over drains, or even as "
"a filter."
msgstr "排水路の覆い、あるいはフィルターとして使われる足場です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A wooden floor created from boards, packed tightly together and nailed down."
"  Common on patios."
msgstr "木の板を隙間なく敷き詰めて釘で打ち付けた床です。テラスなどでよく用いられています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A wooden gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but"
" not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr "狭い隙間に渡して使う、木製の通路です。床の役割は十分に果たせる強度ですが、追加の床材を支えられるほど頑丈ではありません。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of common poured concrete, damaged by frost heaves and large cracks "
"due to lack of maintenance."
msgstr "公共区画に敷かれたコンクリートは氷結によって損傷し、整備不足のために大きなひびが入っています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "upturned dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of loose dirt, not easily traversable.  If examined more closely, "
"it's quite favorable for planting seeds and the like."
msgstr "土が耕されており、通過に時間が掛かります。種などを植えるのに非常に適しています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elevator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "An elevator section of the flight deck."
msgstr "飛行甲板のエレベーター部分です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient floor made from carefully placed rebar and poured "
"concrete, capable of providing protection from the elements.  As for the "
"matching roof, it still requires supporting walls, otherwise it may very "
"well cave in."
msgstr "規則正しく並べた鉄筋にコンクリートを注入して作られた、風雨を防ぐ非常に頑丈な床です。揃いの屋根は壁の支えがなければ、当然崩落します。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gelatinous ground"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An incursion of a large area of otherworldly substrate, it feels like "
"walking on hardened gelatin."
msgstr "広大な面積の土地が奇妙な物体に侵食されています。固まったゼラチンの上を歩いているような感覚です。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "odd fault"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An unnaturally humanoid-shaped hole, it seems oddly familiar.  You feel a "
"strange urge to examine it closer, as if it belongs to you somehow."
msgstr ""
"この異様な人型の穴を、何故かよく知っているような気がします。自分のための穴があるような気がして、もっと近寄って見てみたいという奇妙な衝動に駆られます。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls."
msgstr "スリップや転倒のリスクを軽減する、高品質で強靭な金属でできた格子模様のフローリングです。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "It's dirt, suitable for digging or tilling."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "rocky soil"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Many stones are protruding from beneath the ground.  This would not be good "
"farmland."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Streaks of carefully aligned yellow paint mark the road to inform drivers "
"not to cross.  No one is enforcing these rules anymore."
msgstr ""
"丁寧に並んだ黄色いペンキの縞模様は、運転者が道路をはみ出さないよう注意するために付けられた印です。こんなルールを強制する者はもう誰一人残っていません。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "forest floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"The soil here is tightly packed around a network of tree roots and buried "
"under a thick mat of rotting leaves and other debris."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_TERRAIN_FAULT" in terrain "odd
#. fault"'s examine action
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"This wall is perfectly vertical.  Odd, twisted holes are set in it, leading "
"as far back into the solid rock as you can see.  The holes are humanoid in "
"shape, but with long, twisted, distended limbs."
msgstr ""
"この壁は完全な垂直になっています。壁には歪んだ妙な穴が開いており、かなり奥まで続いているようです。穴は人間のような形をしていますが、手足の部分が長く伸び、捻じれています。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pedestrian crossing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"White polymer lines painted on the pavement which indicate places where "
"pedestrians should cross the road."
msgstr "歩行者が車道を横断する場所を示す、舗装道路に塗られた白い樹脂塗料の線です。"

