#. ~ Description of variant "pilgrim hat" of item "wizard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A broad-brimmed black hat with a buckled belt around the crown.  It's a "
"cheap replica of the kind ahistorically associated with the pilgrims who "
"settled at Plymouth Rock."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "kerchief"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A cotton bandana worn over the head.  It can be adjusted to cover the mouth "
"and nose instead."
msgstr "綿製のバンダナです。埃や汚染物質を多少防ぎ、口を暖めます。"

#. ~ Description of "baseball cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A cotton cap with a rounded crown, an adjustable strap, and a long visor.  "
"It shields your eyes from the sun and provides a little bit of warmth.  "
"Traditionally worn by baseball players."
msgstr ""
"丸みを帯びたクラウン、サイズを調節できるストラップ、長いバイザーが特徴的な綿製の帽子です。日差しから目を保護し、多少寒さを防ぎます。野球選手が着用する伝統的なキャップです。"

#. ~ Description of "tricorne"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A design that goes back to the founding of the thirteen colonies, this is a "
"wide-brimmed oiled leather hat pinned up on three sides to make a "
"distinctive three-pointed design."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "golf cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A flat, short-brimmed cap, commonly worn by golfers."
msgstr "ダイバーがよく着用している3mm厚ネオプレン製フードです。"

#. ~ Description of "porkpie hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A flat-topped hat with circular indent and a narrow brim.  Most popular in "
"the 40s and 50s, still common among those in the mod scene, hipsters, and "
"people named Heisenberg."
msgstr ""
"丸まった短いつばを持つ天辺が平らな帽子です。最も流行したのは1940～50年代ですが、モッズ・スタイルの若者やファッションに敏感なヒップスター、ハイゼンベルグという通り名をもつ男は未だにこの帽子を愛用しているようです。"

#. ~ Description of "French maid hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A frilly white headpiece."
msgstr "フリルの付いた白いヘッドピースです。"

#. ~ Description of "summer hard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A hard plastic hat worn at construction and industrial sites, with a sun "
"shield tucked on top to keep the glare out of your eyes.  Protects your eyes"
" from the harsh sun, although it makes ear muffs unattachable to the hard "
"hat itself."
msgstr "内側に簡易フードがついた、建設現場や工場で着用するプラスチック製のヘルメットです。ある程度快適に着用でき、首筋を太陽や雨から保護します。"

#. ~ Description of "hard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A hard plastic hat worn at construction and industrial sites.  Provides "
"excellent protection from cuts and percussion."
msgstr "建設現場や工場で着用する硬質プラスチック製のヘルメットです。斬撃や打撃に対して優れた防御力を発揮します。"

#. ~ Description of "fur hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A hat made from the pelts of animals.  Extremely warm."
msgstr "動物の毛皮から作られた、極めて暖かい帽子です。"

#. ~ Description of "straw hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A hat woven out of straw.  Its brim helps keep the sun out of your eyes."
msgstr "藁を編んで作った帽子です。つばが付いており、日差しから目を守ります。"

#. ~ Description of "eboshi"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A high, black cap with a very narrow top.  Traditionally worn by Shinto "
"priests."
msgstr "幅が狭く、背の高い黒い帽子です。日本の神職が行事の際に被ります。"

#. ~ Description of variant "witch hat" of item "wizard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A pointed black hat with a broad brim."
msgstr "魔女によく似合う、先端が尖った帽子です。"

#. ~ Description of "wizard hat"
#. ~ Description of variant "wizard hat" of item "wizard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A pointed blue hat with stars stitched into it."
msgstr "星形が刺繍された青いとんがり帽子です。着用すると最大マナ容量が上昇します。"

#. ~ Description of "Santa hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A red hat with white faux fur trim, commonly used by bearded men on "
"Christmas."
msgstr "髭面の男がクリスマスによく着用している、白いフェイクファーで縁取られた赤い帽子です。"

#. ~ Description of "hunting cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A red plaid hunting cap with ear flaps.  Notably warm."
msgstr "赤いチェック柄の耳当てが付いた非常に暖かいハンチング帽です。"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum foil hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of aluminum foil that has been molded into a form-fitting hat.  "
"Perfect for protecting yourself from the government, Illuminati, aliens, and"
" THEM."
msgstr "頭の形状にぴったり合うように成形したアルミ箔の帽子です。政府、イルミナティ、エイリアン、そして奴らから身を守るのに最適です。"

#. ~ Description of "patrol cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A simple round cap in a camouflage pattern.  Often used by the military when"
" helmets aren't needed.  Its brim helps keep the sun out of your eyes."
msgstr "ヘルメットが必要ない状況で兵士が着用する、迷彩柄のシンプルな丸天帽子です。つばが付いており、日差しから目を守ります。"

#. ~ Description of "newsboy cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A slouching wool cap with a short front brim, traditionally associated with "
"newspaper delivery boys.  Quite warm."
msgstr ""
"前方につばがあるウールの大きな帽子です。米国では新聞配達の少年が被っていた事からニュースボーイキャップとも呼ばれています。被るとかなり暖かいです。"

#. ~ Description of "zucchetto"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A small, crimson skullcap.  Traditionally worn by Catholic priests."
msgstr "真紅の小さな丸い帽子です。カトリックの司祭が伝統的に着用します。"

#. ~ Description of "knit hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A snug-fitting wool hat.  Very warm."
msgstr "頭部にフィットするウールの帽子です。被るととても暖かいです。"

#. ~ Description of "beret"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A soft cap that fits snugly about the head with a bit of slack on top."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wool beret"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A soft felt cap that fits snugly about the head with a bit of slack on top."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "faux fur hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A stylish hat made of faux fur.  Like real fur, but without the suffering, "
"if the tag is to be believed.  Very warm."
msgstr ""
"フェイクファー製のお洒落な帽子です。本物の毛皮そっくりですが、付いているタグを信じるならば、殺生なしで作られた物と言えます。非常に暖かい着心地です。"

#. ~ Description of "kippah"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A thin, rounded skullcap.  A traditional headdress in Judaism."
msgstr "皿のような形をした小さくて薄い帽子です。ユダヤ教の伝統的な民族衣装です。"

#. ~ Description of "toque"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A traditional chef's hat, standing tall and proud against the vulgarities of"
" the world."
msgstr "伝統的なシェフの帽子です。無作法な世の中に逆らうが如く、そそり立っています。"

#. ~ Description of "mail carrier hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"A traditional mail carrier's cap, with the US postal service logo "
"embroidered on the front above the plastic brim.  A symbol of a bygone "
"world."
msgstr ""
"伝統的な郵便配達員のつば付き帽子です。プラスチック製のキャップの前頭部にはアメリカ合衆国郵便公社のロゴが刺繍されていますが、もはや過去のシンボルです。"

#. ~ Description of "beanie"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A warm knit hat."
msgstr "ニット帽"

#. ~ Description of "chaplet"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A wreath headdress made from plant material woven into a ring."
msgstr "植物を編んで輪にした頭飾りです。"

#. ~ Description of "boonie hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"Also called a \"bucket hat.\" Often used in the military.  Its wide brim "
"helps keep the sun out of your eyes."
msgstr "「バケットハット」とも呼ばれ、軍でよく使われています。広いつばが付いており、日差しから目を守ります。"

#. ~ Description of "eight point cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"Also known as a utility cover or utility cap, this is an eight pointed hat "
"with a baseball-style visor at the front.  Commonly worn by Marines and "
"sailors, this hat is the standard headwear of both the United States Marine "
"Corps and Navy."
msgstr ""
"ユーティリティカバーやユーティリティキャップとも呼ばれる、前面に野球帽のようなバイザーが付いた八角帽です。アメリカの海兵隊や海軍の標準的な頭部装備であり、海兵隊員や水兵がよく着用しています。"

#. ~ Description of "drinking hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"An improvised harness that can be worn over other headgear or by itself, "
"made from two small liquid containers, a rubber hose, a bundle of steel "
"wire, and some cordage.  A convenient and simple device for hands-free "
"drinking, though it's not watertight and would spill if you put it into your"
" backpack."
msgstr ""
"小型液体容器2本、ゴムホース、鋼鉄ワイヤーで作った、他の頭部防具の上から、あるいは直接頭に着用できる簡素なヘッドバンドです。原理は単純ながら手を使わずに飲み物を飲める便利な道具ですが、密閉はできないため荷物に入れようとすると中身がこぼれます。"

#. ~ Description of "bowler hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"An old-fashioned gentleman's cap with a domed crown and a short, rounded "
"brim."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sombrero"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"An orange felt sombrero with traditional white and yellow hand stitching.  "
"The wide brim keeps the sun out of your eyes, and a thin strap hooks around "
"your chin."
msgstr "白と黄色の伝統的な刺繍がされた、フェルト製のオレンジ色のソンブレロです。顎に細い紐で固定して着用し、広いつばが日光から目を守ります。"

#. ~ Description of "turban"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"Cloth wound around the head, worn by people of many cultures worldwide."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "kerchief"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "Cover mouth"
msgstr "口に着用する"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "French maid hat"
msgid_plural "French maid hats"
msgstr[0] "ホワイトブリム"

#. ~ Description of "noise canceling headgear"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid ""
"Padding over your ears, kept in place by some string.  Blocks incoming "
"sounds."
msgstr "当て布を耳の上から紐で固定して着用します。外からの音を遮断します。"

