#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin carbine" of gun "Mosin-Nagant M44 carbine"
#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin-Nagant M44 carbine" of item "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"The Model 44 is the carbine-sized variant of the standard 1891/30.  It has a"
" shorter barrel, making it weaker than the 1891/30, but easier to carry.  "
"This weapon also comes with an integrated side-folding bayonet."
msgstr ""
"モシン・ナガン1891/30の派生型で、銃身が短くなっているカービン仕様のものです。短くなった分威力でやや標準型に劣りますが、持ち運びが容易です。側面に折り畳める銃剣が内蔵されています。"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin battle rifle" of gun "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30
#. rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30 rifle" of item "Mosin battle
#. rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"The Mosin-Nagant 1891/30 is a bolt-action, internal magazine-fed military "
"rifle, developed by the Russian Empire and later used and perfected by the "
"Soviet Union."
msgstr "固定弾倉式の軍用ボルトアクションライフルです。帝政ロシア時代に開発され、後にソビエト連邦によって改良されました。"

#. ~ Description of gun "PSL rifle"
#. ~ Description of "PSL rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"The Romanian PSL is a designated marksman's rifle developed by Romania after"
" political tensions with Soviet Russia forced them to develop their own "
"alternative to the SVD."
msgstr "政治的緊張状態にあったソビエト連邦のSVDに代わる独自の銃の開発を余儀なくされたルーマニアが生み出した、軍用マークスマンライフルです。"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin battle rifle" of gun "Mosin-Nagant
#. 1891/30-EBR rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR rifle" of item "Mosin
#. battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"This Mosin-Nagant has exchanged the classic wooden stock for a modern "
"synthetic model, carefully balanced to the same weight and handling, to "
"allow support for modern accessories."
msgstr ""
"古典的な木製の銃床を現代的な合成樹脂モデルに換装したモシン・ナガンです。現代的なアクセサリーに対応しつつ、重量やバランスが原型と同じになるよう慎重に調整してあります。"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin carbine" of gun "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR
#. carbine"
#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR carbine" of item "Mosin
#. carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"This carbine packs the classic Mosin-Nagant Model 44 action in a modern-day "
"stock capable of accepting modifications."
msgstr "古典的なモシン・ナガンM44の操作性に現代的な銃床をプラスし、更に様々なアクセサリーを取り付けられる作りになっています。"

#. ~ Description of variant "PPSh-41 submachine gun" of gun "PPSh-41
#. submachine gun"
#. ~ Description of variant "PPSh-41 submachine gun" of item "PPSh-41
#. submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid ""
"A bulky and simple Second World War submachine gun of Russian manufacture, "
"composed from a basic wooden buttstock, steel barrel shroud, and the hopes "
"and prayers of Soviet soldiers under threat of German invasion.  Designed "
"for mass production with limited materials, the weapon is notable for its "
"high-capacity drum magazines, capability of rapidly depleting said "
"magazines, and vicious 7.62x25mm chambering."
msgstr ""
"第二次世界大戦でドイツ軍の侵攻にさらされたソ連兵の希望と祈りが込められた、木製の銃床と鋼鉄製のバレルシュラウドをベースに構成されている、ロシア製のシンプルで嵩張るサブマシンガンです。限られた材料で大量生産できるように設計されており、大容量のドラム型弾倉と、その中に装填された危険な7.62x25mm弾を一瞬で消費する性能が特徴です。"

#. ~ Description of gun "Tokarev handgun"
#. ~ Description of "Tokarev handgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid ""
"A symbol of Soviet pride and favored sidearm of Red Army officers, this is a"
" compact pistol firing the punchy 7.62x25mm cartridge.  featuring an "
"uncomfortable grip angle reminiscent of brandishing an unusually irate "
"capital L at one's opponents, it is nevertheless a commendably accurate and "
"durable handgun."
msgstr ""
"高威力の7.62x25mm弾を発射するコンパクトなこのピストルは、ソ連の誇りの象徴であり、赤軍将校が愛用していたサイドアームです。グリップの角度が非常に扱い辛く、まるで敵に対して大文字のLを振りかざしているように見えますが、それはともかく精度と耐久性は折り紙付きです。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#. ~ Variant name of gun "PPSh-41 submachine gun"
#. ~ Variant name of item "PPSh-41 submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid "PPSh-41 submachine gun"
msgid_plural "PPSh-41 submachine guns"
msgstr[0] "サブマシンガン(7.62x25mm/PPSh-41)"

#. ~ Description of gun "PPSh-41 submachine gun"
#. ~ Description of "PPSh-41 submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid ""
"The Soviet-made PPSh-41 is a mass-produced selective-fire submachine gun.  "
"It has a relatively high rate of fire."
msgstr "ソ連が大量製造した、セレクティブ・ファイア機構付きのサブマシンガンです。発射速度は比較的速くなっています。"

#. ~ Description of variant "Tokarev handgun" of gun "Tokarev TT-33 pistol"
#. ~ Description of variant "Tokarev TT-33 pistol" of item "Tokarev handgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid ""
"The Tokarev TT-33 is an antique Russian semiautomatic pistol, famous for its"
" durability, accuracy, and uncomfortable grip angle.  It was chambered for "
"the 7.62x25mm due to the popularity of the C96 pistol among Russian "
"revolutionaries."
msgstr ""
"トカレフTT-33は耐久性、精度、持ちにくいグリップ角度で有名なロシアの古いセミオートマチックピストルです。当時はロシアの革命家たちの間でモーゼルC96が流行っていたため、それと同じ7.62x25mm弾を装填できるようになっています。"

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Tokarev handgun"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Tokarev handgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid "Tokarev TT-33 pistol"
msgid_plural "Tokarev TT-33 pistols"
msgstr[0] "ハンドガン(7.62x25mm/ﾄｶﾚﾌTT-33)"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid "Tokarev handgun"
msgid_plural "Tokarev handguns"
msgstr[0] "ハンドガン(7.62x25mm/ﾄｶﾚﾌ)"

