#. ~ Description of "booby trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A crude explosive device triggered by a piece of string.  Use it to set it "
"up and wait for some poor bastard to trigger it."
msgstr "繋がれた紐を引っ張ると起爆する簡素な爆発罠です。使用して設置し、哀れな犠牲者が引っ掛かるのを待ちましょう。"

#. ~ Description of "loose glass caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A handful of glass shards glued together to expose all their sharp edges.  "
"If an unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get cut."
msgstr "尖った部分が上を向くように接着したガラス片です。何も知らない犠牲者が上に乗れば、足を切り刻むでしょう。"

#. ~ Description of "loose teeth caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A handful of small impossibly-sharp teeth glued together.  If an "
"unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a tooth through the foot."
msgstr "信じられないほど鋭い歯を集めて固めた塊です。何も知らない犠牲者が上に乗れば、足に歯が刺さるでしょう。"

#. ~ Description of "loose caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A handful of small metal objects covered with many sharp points.  If an "
"unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a spine through the foot."
msgstr "沢山の鋭い棘で覆われている、小さな金属製の物体です。何も知らない犠牲者が上に乗れば、足に棘が刺さるでしょう。"

#. ~ Description of "tripwire trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A length of thin string with some affixing tools on either end.  It must be "
"placed across a doorway or other thin passage to function.  Its purpose is "
"to trip up trespassers, causing them to stumble and possibly hurt themselves"
" slightly."
msgstr "両端に取り付け部品が付いた細い紐です。出入り口や狭い通路などに設置する必要があります。侵入者を引っ掛けて転ばせ、軽いダメージを与えます。"

#. ~ Description of "M14 land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A pressure-activated explosive device colloquially known as a \"toepopper.\""
"  These small land mines were once only found along the Korean demilitarized"
" zone, but were quite controversially deployed en masse across the United "
"States in an attempt to deter the inexorable advance of the walking dead."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bubble wrap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of plastic covered with air-filled bubbles.  Use it to set it on the"
" ground, creating a trap that will warn you with noise when something steps "
"on it."
msgstr "表面に気泡が並んでいるビニールシートです。使用すると地面に設置し、誰かに踏まれると音を立てて警戒を促します。"

#. ~ Description of "light snare kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A simple loop snare, comprising a carefully wound loop of string, two anchor"
" points, and a tool to hammer them in.  It is suitable for immobilizing only"
" small animals.  It has no means of harming its target, as live meat lasts "
"longer."
msgstr ""
"紐を丹念に巻いて作った輪と2つの固定具、固定に使う道具が揃った、小動物の捕獲に適したくくり罠一式です。生きたまま捕らえた方が肉が新鮮なため、捕獲対象にダメージは与えられません。"

#. ~ Description of "crossbow trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A simple tripwire attached to the trigger of a loaded crossbow.  When the "
"tripwire is pulled, the crossbow fires.  Only a single bolt can be used, "
"after which the trap is disabled."
msgstr ""
"クロスボウの引き金に仕掛け線を括り付けただけのシンプルな罠です。仕掛け線を引くと、クロスボウが発射されます。ボルトは1本しか装填できないため、罠は一度しか作動しません。"

#. ~ Description of "shotgun trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A simple tripwire attached to the trigger of a loaded double slam-fire "
"shotgun.  When the tripwire is pulled, the shotgun fires.  Two shells are "
"loaded; the first time the trigger is pulled, one or both shells may be "
"discharged."
msgstr ""
"装填済みの2連ショットガンの引き金に仕掛け線を括り付けただけのシンプルな罠です。弾は2発装填されており、作動すると1発または2発が発射されます。"

#. ~ Description of "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid ""
"A spring-loaded pair of steel jaws connected to a sensitive pressure plate."
"  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will ensnare and "
"damage anything that steps on it.  If you are carrying a shovel, you will "
"have the option of burying it."
msgstr ""
"バネで固定された一対の鋼鉄製の爪が、感度の高い圧力板に繋がっています。地面に設置すると、上に乗った者を強く挟んでダメージを与える罠になります。シャベルを所持していれば、設置する際に埋めて隠せます。"

#. ~ "bury_question" action message of item "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the beartrap?"
msgstr "トラバサミを埋めますか？"

#. ~ "bury_question" action message of item "M14 land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the land mine?"
msgstr "地雷を埋めますか？"

