#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"I think it's possible, but ultimately unknowable.  What matters now is "
"survival and actually fighting the monsters that are trying to kill us.  We "
"shouldn't dwell on crazy theories."
msgstr ""
"可能性はあると思うけど、考えたって結局答えは分からない。今一番大事なのは生き延びること、そして現実世界で襲いかかってくる怪物に立ち向かうことだろう。おかしな理論に囚われてばかりじゃダメだ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"I think you might be right.  The government probably does have something to "
"do with it."
msgstr "その考えには一理ある。きっとアメリカ政府も何か関係しているんだろう。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"I thought we could team up.  It sounded like a good place to stay safe."
msgstr "協力できると思っただけだ。ここは安全に過ごせる場所だからね。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"I uh… found my way inside it a while ago.  The door was already open.  I "
"kinda went through it already assuming whoever owned it was dead."
msgstr "その...以前、入ったことがあるんだ。入口は開いていた。てっきり家主は死んだと思って、気にせず入ってしまった。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"I'd have to be absolutely <dumb> to give up the location of my stash to "
"someone I barely know.  For all I know you'd just kill me and take it all "
"for yourself!  Better luck next time, pal."
msgstr ""
"ほぼ他人のような奴に隠れ家を教えるなんて、途方もない<dumb>じゃないか。私を殺してシェルターを独り占めする気だろう！次はもっと上手くやることだな。"

