#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Why else would I ask about your shelter?  I don't need your gear.  I don't "
"need your help.  Look around you!  I'm tracking down the last free thinkers "
"who have been putting the puzzle pieces together.  It's YOU I'm after!"
msgstr ""
"他にシェルターのことを聞く理由があるか？ここの道具など必要ない。お前の助けも必要ない。考えても見ろ！私はパズルのピースを組み立てているんだ。自由思想家の生き残りを追い詰めるためにな。そう、お前のことだよ！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Why not?  Now that it's all finally come to a head, maybe some of your "
"theories are right."
msgstr "どうして？陰謀が真実だったと証明できる状況がようやく訪れたかもしれないのに。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm just messing with you, don't worry.  What, can't take a joke?"
msgstr "ああ、ちょっとからかってみたんだ、悪かった。冗談だよ、分かるだろう？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, but they put the secret room in their advertising.  Not really a "
"secret then, is it?"
msgstr "ああ、でも、広告チラシに隠し部屋付きって書いてあったんだ。それって、何も隠せてないよな？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "Yeah, it does seem a little grim…  Let's keep moving for now."
msgstr "ああ、現実は辛いけど...とにかく動き続けるしかない。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, listen, just keep your questions to yourself.  I don't trust you and "
"you shouldn't trust me, either."
msgstr "ああ、そうかい、もう金輪際あんたの声は聞きたくない。あんたのことは今後まったく信用しないし、こっちのことも信用しないでくれ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "Yeah…?  I didn't realize it bothered you so much."
msgstr "ええっと...？そんなに怒るとは思わなかった、ごめん。"

#. ~ Player message in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You approach the LMOE and do as you were told, prying back a thin piece of "
"metal atop the doorframe, revealing an opening.  You reach inside and grab a"
" handle attached to a wire, pull hard on it, and hear a heavy metal *clunk*."
"  The door is open."
msgstr ""
"LMOEシェルターに近付き、言われた通りにドア枠上部の金属部を動かすと、空洞が現れました。内部に手を入れ、ワイヤーで吊られたハンドルを強く引っ張ると、*ガチャリ*と重い金属音が響き渡りました。ドアのロックが解除されたようです。"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.  Comes up a lot and could use more
#. variety.
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json data/json/npcs/talk_tags.json
msgid "You got it."
msgstr "ああ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"You know, the elites.  The ones who have always had control will continue "
"having control, no matter what it costs.  If it means destroying everything "
"to be king of the ashes, they'll do it.  I used to think it was China, for "
"sure, but I'm not so sure anymore.  I figured they would probably be here by"
" now, putting on their crown.  Maybe they're still waiting to make their "
"move…"
msgstr ""
"それはもちろん、特権階級だ。常に支配者層にいる奴らは、どんな代償を払ってでも支配者層に居座り続ける。すべてを破壊して灰の中の玉座に就くことになっても、別に構わないのさ。以前は、間違いなく中国こそが黒幕だと思っていたけれど、今は状況が違うのかもしれない。今頃はどこかで王冠をかぶってふんぞり返っているのか、それとも行動を起こす機会を伺っているのか..."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
