#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You said you could tell me more about the shelter if I wanted.  How did "
"these things get built?"
msgstr "シェルターについて詳しく教えてくれると言っていたな。どうやって作ったんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "You sure do."
msgstr "それはよかった。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You think that's funny?!  Some of us watched the warning signs for years.  "
"All the news, all the violence and the secret plots…  Now the dead are "
"walking, reality itself is tearing apart, and you're making jokes like "
"that?!"
msgstr ""
"何が面白いんだ！？警告のサインを何年も見てきたんだ。ニュースや暴行事件、秘密の計画...今や死者が歩き始め、現実が壊れてきているのに、そんな下らない冗談を言うのか！？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"You wouldn't keep ALL your tricks and secrets from me, though, would you?  "
"After everything we've been through?"
msgstr "私に仕掛けを隠しておく意味は、もうないんじゃないかな？ここも共有することになるんだろう？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"You're not really a good liar.  I built that thing like a fortress.  No one "
"would just break into it."
msgstr "嘘をつくのが下手だな。あのシェルターは要塞だ。無理やり入るなんて不可能だ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
