msgstr "モジュール式平野拠点について教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Tell me about pottery cottage camps."
msgstr "陶芸工房拠点について教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Tell me about radio tower camps."
msgstr "電波塔拠点について教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Tell me about small sealab camps."
msgstr "淡水研究所拠点について教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Tell me how faction camps have changed."
msgstr "拠点の仕組みの変更点を教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Tell me how faction camps work."
msgstr "拠点の仕組みを教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Tell me more about camp missions."
msgstr "拠点での任務について教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Tell me more about faction camps and food."
msgstr "拠点と食料について教えてほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Thanks, let's go back to talking about camps."
msgstr "ありがとう、拠点についての他の話をしよう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"The bare bones camp is the most flexible kind of camp as you can build them "
"anywhere while still having access to almost all camp capabilities, leaving "
"it completely up to you how you design them (the missed functionality is "
"tied to the construction of a radio tower).  You start by ordering the "
"companion to build the camp, then construct a bulletin board within it "
"yourself or by ordering your companion to make a zone construction for it, "
"after which you can use the board to order companions to execute camp "
"missions without construction preconditions.  You still have to meet all the"
" usual restrictions for companion crafting missions, such as access to fire,"
" tools, etc, but facilities constructed by you or your companions should be "
"available for crafting provided you have covered them with Camp: Supply "
"zones.  How you want to construct the camp in your chosen location is up to "
"you, with construction zones available should you want to give the task to "
"your companions."
msgstr ""
"フリー拠点は、ほぼすべての拠点機能を備えながらどこにでも作れる、最も柔軟なタイプの拠点で、完全に好きなように設計できる(電波塔の建設に関連する機能だけは備わっていない)。まずは仲間に拠点を作るよう指示し、拠点の範囲内の好きな位置に掲示板を自分で設置するか、区域管理機能を使って建設を指示する。完成した掲示板を調べれば、建物などがなくても仲間に任務を与えられるようになる。仲間にアイテムを製作させる任務では、火元や道具など通常の製作と同じ要件を満たさないといけないが、「拠点:"
" 物資」の区域内に自分や仲間が建設した設備も活用できる。どのような拠点にするかは、すべてあなた次第だ。建設区域を設定して仲間に作業を任せてもいい。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"The faction camp system allows you to use companions to take over existing "
"buildings or construct new buildings and use them to extend the usefulness "
"of your allies.  When you have a faction camp, you can order your companions"
" to perform missions, such as crafting new items, building up the camp, "
"hunting for food, or recruiting more allies.  Faction camps also simplify "
"some aspects of managing your companions."
msgstr ""
"派閥の拠点は、仲間のNPCに指示して既存の建物を改築したり、新しく建物を建てたりして作る。拠点があれば、仲間の役割を更に増やせるんだ。例えば、アイテム製作や拠点の改良、食料調達、他のNPCを探して勧誘するなど、様々な任務を命じられる。派閥の拠点を作れば、仲間の行動を楽に管理することもできる。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"The modular field camp is the second most flexible kind of camp, but they require a lot of time and resources to build.  There are actually two different versions with slightly different layouts.  With both versions you start with an empty field which can be a field, hay field, farm field, or dirt road on a field, and build up from nothing.  You have a range of different building materials available from which buildings can be constructed, and different sections can be constructed from different materials to make the most of what you have available.\n"
"  You start by building a lean-to and a bed in the northeast corner of the central camp, and then typically add a cooking facility to it, and expand out until you have a small shelter for two people.  When the first building is complete, you can expand the camp in a variety of ways:\n"
"  1.  Version 1 allows building up to 5 more rooms or shacks with a maximum of 3 on each side of the camp that increases to a total of 8 with version 2.\n"
"  2.  You can build a central building in the south half of the camp, between the rooms in version 1, with version 2 having the central building in the center, shaping the camp into an 'H'.  The central building will act as a command center, allowing your camp to perform hunting, recruiting, and combat patrol missions.\n"
"  3.  In version 1 only you can dig trenches on all sides of the camp, which can possibly connect to the rooms on the sides to minimize the amount of trenching you need to do.\n"
"  4.  You can build various small features such as root cellars to preserve food or a radio tower to make it easier to recruit more companions.\n"
"  With each new construction in a modular camp can being able to be made from a different material you aren't constrained by what you start with.  If limited by resources, tents are a fast alternative way to provide shelter, but fragile and likely to get destroyed by the first zombie stumbling in, however the central building must still be made from a 'real' building material."
msgstr ""
"モジュール式平野拠点は二番目に自由度の高い拠点だが、構築には多くの時間と資材が必要だ。実は、レイアウトが微妙に異なる2タイプのバージョンがある。どちらのタイプも、平野、牧草地、農地、未舗装道路などの何もない場所に一から建物を作ることになる。建築資材にも選択肢が用意されている。その時余っている資材を都度選んで建設を進めれば、手持ちの資源を最大限に活用できるだろう。\n"
"  拠点の北東区画に簡単な小屋とベッドを作り、通常はその次に調理設備をを追加し、2人用の小さなシェルターができるまで拠点を充実させる。そこまで改良が終わったら、拠点構築の様々な選択肢が選べるようになる:\n"
"  1. レイアウト1では拠点の東西に最大3つずつ、合計で最大5つの住居を作れる。レイアウト2では合計8つまで住居を増やせる。\n"
"  2. 中央棟を建てる。レイアウト1では拠点中央の南寄りの、個室の間に位置する。レイアウト2では中心部に建て、H字型の建物になる。中央棟は指令室として機能し、拠点で狩猟、仲間の勧誘、巡回の任務を指示できるようになる。\n"
"  3. レイアウト1では、拠点の四方すべてに塹壕を掘ることができる。部屋の壁と接している面は、塹壕を掘る必要がない。\n"
"  4. 食料を保存する貯蔵穴や仲間を増やしやすくする電波塔など、様々な機能をもつ設備を追加する。\n"
"  前述のとおり、モジュール式拠点内の建築物はそれぞれ異なる素材の資材を選べるので、最初に選んだ素材で後々困ることはない。資源が不足しているなら、テントを資材に選べば手早く住居を増やせる。ただし、テントは壊れやすく、ゾンビに壊されてしまう可能性もある。中央棟は必ず「本物の」建築資材で作らなければならないことは覚えておこう。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Wait, let's go back over from the start."
msgstr "ちょっと待って、もう一度最初から説明してほしい。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Wait, we can talk with radios?"
msgstr "待って、無線機で会話できるのか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#: data/json/npcs/common_chat/TALK_COMMON_ALLY.json
msgid "We need to abandon this camp."
msgstr "この拠点を放棄しよう。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Well, then.  Let's get back to work."
msgstr "そうか、分かった。さあ行こうか。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "Well, until we go there, let's talk about camps more."
msgstr "じゃあ、目的の場所を見つける前に、拠点についてもっと話しておこう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "What about faction camps?"
msgstr "拠点について何の話をしようか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid "What do you mean by angry?"
msgstr "「不満に思う」とはどういう意味？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"When you assign a companion to a faction camp mission, they'll disappear while they go do whatever you want them to do.  When the duration of the mission has elapsed, you'll see a new mission on the bulletin board to have them return and complete the mission by upgrading your camp, returning their hunting kills, dropping off whatever they were crafting, or whatever else the mission results are.\n"
"  There are all kinds of faction camp missions: building up the camp, recruiting new allies, hunting and trapping game, scrounging for materials, farming, disassembling cars, and more.  Not all activities can be done at every camp - you may need to build some additional buildings, or expand the camp, to get access to some missions.\n"
"  Some faction camp missions can be duplicated by companion activities, but building up the camp can only be done via faction camp missions, as only completion of camp construction missions are recognized as fulfillment of those goals.\n"
"  You assign missions by interacting with the bulletin board.  You'll see a list of available missions for your central camp tile.  If your camp has expansions, you can tab through the expansions to see the available missions at each expansion.\n"
"  Remember, companions on camp missions need to be fed, and will become angry if they complete a mission but there isn't any food in the larder.\n"
"  There is one special mission called 'Emergency Recall'.  You can use this to retrieve any companion on a faction camp mission, but this cancels the mission and wastes any resources used on it.  Only use it to recover allies when something has gone really wrong with your camp and you can't get them to come back any other way."
msgstr ""
"拠点の任務を割り当てられた仲間は、任務中は姿を消す。任務の期間が過ぎると、掲示板に仲間を呼び戻すという項目が追加される。それを選択すれば任務は完了となって、拠点の改良、狩りや製作で得たアイテムの入手など、任務の結果が反映され、仲間も戻ってくる。\n"
"  拠点で割り当てられる任務は、拠点改良、新たな仲間の勧誘、狩猟や罠猟、資材調達、農作業、車両解体など様々だ。でも、全ての任務がすぐにできる訳じゃない...例えば特定の建物の建設や拠点の拡張を先にこなさないとできない任務もある。\n"
"任務の中には、仲間に直接話しかけて同じような仕事を頼めるものもあるが、拠点の構築に関する任務は拠点でしか指示できないし、建物などは複数の任務をすべて完了して初めて完成したことになる。\n"
"  任務は拠点内の掲示板を使って割り当てる。掲示板を調べれば、中央拠点の任務一覧が表示されるはずだ。拠点を拡張しているなら、タブキーを押せば各拡張施設の任務一覧が表示される。\n"
"  任務を遂行する仲間には備蓄食料が不可欠だ。任務を終えて帰ってきても、備蓄食料が不十分だと不満に思うことは忘れないで。\n"
"  任務の中には「緊急帰還」という特殊なものがある。これを実行すれば任務中の仲間はすぐに帰ってくるが、任務はキャンセルされ、それまでに任務で消費した資源などは帰ってこない。拠点で何か問題が発生して、他に帰還手段がない場合のみ、この任務を選択して仲間を帰還させよう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a fire lookout tower.  Fire lookout towers often have fields surrounding them.\n"
"  The base camp starts in an established building, and provides a full set of base camp missions, but the number of construction upgrades is limited to a pair of dual bed rooms, a well, a root cellar, and a radio tower.  This makes it a camp that allows you to get the camp setup done with quickly so you can focus on other things."
msgstr ""
"火災監視塔に派閥の拠点を作る利点は、監視塔の周囲が平野である場合が多いことだ。\n"
"  元々の建物をそのまま使えるから、拠点を作ってすぐにいくつかの任務を指示できるようになる。改良は2台のベッドを置く寝室が2つと、他には井戸、貯蔵穴、電波塔だけだ。改良を早く終わらせて他のことに集中したいなら、この拠点を選ぼう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a helipad facility, where you're provided "
"with water purification and cooking facilities from the beginning and can "
"expand with a root cellar, butchering rack, a radio tower, and 4 beds.  A "
"site specific expansion is into the garage, where you're given access to the"
" available appliances."
msgstr ""
"軍のヘリポート施設に派閥の拠点を作ることのが利点は、最初から浄水と調理のための設備が用意されていることだ。改良で増やせるのは貯蔵穴、食肉処理ラック、電波塔、ベッド4台だ。この施設特有の拡張として車両解体場があり、中の設備はそのまま利用できる。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a light industry facility, where you're "
"provided with cooking facilities from the beginning and can expand with a "
"root cellar, butchering rack, well, a radio tower, and beds.  One site "
"specific expansion that's always available is the workshop, where you're "
"given access to the available appliances and can add a drop hammer for "
"companion crafting."
msgstr ""
"軽工場に派閥の拠点を作ると、最初から調理設備が用意されていて、貯蔵穴、食肉処理ラック、井戸、電波塔、ベッドを追加できる。常に選択できる軽工場特有の拡張のひとつが作業場だ。設備をそのまま利用でき、更にドロップハンマーを追加すれば、仲間に様々な製作作業を指示できるようになる。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a lighthouse, where you're provided with "
"water purification and cooking facilities from the beginning and can expand "
"with a root cellar."
msgstr "灯台に派閥の拠点を作ると、浄水や調理用の設備が最初から使える。貯蔵穴を追加することも可能だ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a mansion.  You have four different starting"
" positions available, namely the Fountain Garden, Dance Floor Room, "
"Basketball Room, and Garden with Columns.  Depending on where you set up "
"your base, the following site specific expansions may become available: "
"Entrance 1, Entrance 2, Swimming Pool 1, Bedrooms 1, Unidentified Room, "
"Kitchen 2, Library, Bedrooms 2, Swimming Pool 2, Bar, Living Rooms, Bedroom "
"3, and Kitchen 2.  The Entrances and Swimming Pool 1 provide farming, the "
"Library a limited set of cooking, the Bar a different set, and the Kitchens "
"an extended set of cooking recipes."
msgstr ""
"大邸宅の中に派閥の拠点を作るなら、拠点中央を「噴水庭園」「ダンスフロア」「バスケットコート」「円柱庭園」の4種の中から1つ選ぶことになる。拠点中央の種類によるが、玄関1、玄関2、プール1、寝室1、正体不明の部屋、キッチン2、図書館、寝室2、プール2、バー、リビングルーム、寝室3、キッチン2で大邸宅特有の拡張ができる。玄関とプール1の拡張では農作業、図書館とバーとキッチンの拡張ではそれぞれ異なる料理を仲間に指示できるようになる。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a military outpost, of which there are two "
"versions, 'normal' and 'cross'.  They differ in that the normal version can "
"be expanded with two beds, while the cross version can be expanded with "
"four.  Apart from that, they provide you with the ability to build a root "
"cellar, a butchery rack, a water well, farm plots, a radio tower, and repair"
" the reactor's controller."
msgstr ""
"前哨地内に派閥の拠点を作る場合は、「通常」と「十字型」どちらかを選ぶことになる。通常ではベッドを2台、十字型では4台追加できる。その他には、貯蔵穴、食肉処理ラック、井戸、農地、電波塔の建設、そして原子炉制御装置の修理を実行できる。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a pottery cottage.  Setting up your base "
"there allows you to use the char kiln and clay kiln for crafting.  You can "
"add a butchery rack to the facilities, as well as build blacksmithing "
"facilities."
msgstr "陶芸工房に拠点を作ると、炭焼き窯と陶芸窯をそのまま製作に利用できる。他には食肉処理ラックや鍛冶場を追加することも可能だ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a radio tower, both the version with and the"
" one without an adjacent building on the ground.  Bedroom shacks can be "
"built to host your companions.  You can build a root cellar, a water well, "
"hook yourself up to the radio tower, and fix the tower to get access to "
"extended capabilities."
msgstr ""
"地上に建物がある電波塔とない電波塔、どちらにも派閥の拠点を作れる。寝室用の小屋を建てることで、仲間を休ませることもできるだろう。他には貯蔵穴や井戸の追加、電波塔への接続、設備を改造してさらに機能を増やすこともできる。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in a small sealab facility.  This provides you "
"with access to the air compressor and water purifier appliances on site."
msgstr "淡水研究所に派閥の拠点を作ると、施設内のエアーコンプレッサーや浄水装置を利用できる。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
msgid ""
"You can build a faction camp in any kind of evac shelter.  Evac shelters are everywhere and often have fields surrounding them, so they're a little faster to start than a modular field camp but still make it easy to add expansions.\n"
"  Evac center camps can be built up in several ways.  You basically need to decide between building more bedrooms or adding crafting and cooking space."
msgstr ""
"どんな形状の避難シェルターでも、派閥の拠点は作れる。避難シェルターは数が多いし、平野に囲まれていることも多いから、モジュール式平野拠点より手早く作れて、拡張もしやすい。\n"
"  避難シェルター拠点の構築方針はいくつかある。基本的には、ベッドを増やすか、作業や調理をするスペースを追加するかの二択だ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
msgid "Alright."
msgstr "なるほど。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid "Can I join you?"
msgstr "私も参加できるか？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid ""
"Dangerous?  It may look different, but this land cares and provides for us."
"  We are celebrating with a feast, in fact.  Do you care to join us?"
msgstr "危険？あなたにはそう見えないかも知れませんが、この大地は我々を気遣い、養ってくれています。実際、我々は祝宴の最中です。あなたも参加しては？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid ""
"I don't know what kind of heresy you are spreading, but I'm putting an end "
"to it!"
msgstr "どんな異端の教えを広めているのか知らないが、私が終止符を打ってやる！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid "I have changed my mind, thank you."
msgstr "悪いけど、気が変わった。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgid "I'd… rather not."
msgstr "ちょっと...分からないな。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/TALK_MARLOSS_VOICE.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"I'm a priest or guide of a sort.  I sing the hymns along my companions so "
"that we may learn to live in unity, both with each other and with our ailing"
" world."
msgstr "私は司祭、案内人とも言えますね。調和して生きることを学べるように、仲間と共に賛歌を歌い広めています。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
