msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid ""
"I used to travel a lot before <the_cataclysm>, and I've had this camper with"
" me for a while now.  I was at home when the riots started, so I grabbed "
"everything I could from my house and hopped in the camper.  I nearly wrecked"
" on my way out of town when some crazy people tried to smash my van, but I "
"made it out.  I've been on the move ever since."
msgstr ""
"<the_cataclysm>以前はよく旅行していて、このキャンピングカーもしばらく前から乗っていたんだ。暴動が激しくなってきた頃、家にあるものを全部車に詰め込んで、逃げ出した。街からでる途中で、危うく頭のおかしい奴らに車を壊されそうになったけど、何とか無事に走ってこられた。それ以来、ずっと旅を続けている。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid ""
"I'll be gone here in a day or two, just stopping long enough to get some "
"supplies and fix anything wrong with the camper."
msgstr "一日か二日後だ。物資の調達や車の修理が終わったら、出発する。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Let's take a look."
msgstr "見てみよう。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that collapsed house"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Sweet."
msgstr "そりゃよかった。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that collapsed house"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "That's unfortunate."
msgstr "そりゃ残念だったな。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid ""
"What's in that RV of yours?  Couldn't be anything you need, so hand over "
"your stuff."
msgstr "そのキャンピングカーに何を積んでいる？もう不要だろ、こっちに寄越せ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "When will you be leaving?"
msgstr "いつ出発する？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where did you say you were going again?"
msgstr "次はどこへ行くんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where was the bunker at?"
msgstr "その掩体壕はどの辺りにあった？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where were they at?"
msgstr "その人とはどの辺りで出会った？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"*tips their hat down from their eyes and looks at you blearily.  \"Huh?  "
"Hey, I'm tryin'a sleep here.  I was on night watch."
msgstr "*は帽子を目深にかぶり、くたびれた目でこちらを見ています。「あぁ？ちょっと、こっちは夜番で、今から寝るところだったのに。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Actually I had a little more to trade still."
msgstr "そうだ、他にも取り引きできる物資があったんだ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Always good to do a little trading."
msgstr "物資の取り引きね、任せてくれ。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Are you threatening me?"
msgstr "それは脅しなのか？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Can you give me directions to any of these other survivor groups?"
msgstr "他の生存者集団がいる場所を教えてもらえないか？"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, tells you about being a guard and directs you
#. to free merchants.
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, doesn't have much to say.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Caravan Guard"
msgstr "隊商護衛"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  Feel free to come by and trade, or if "
"you're the type, we might have use for your services as a merc."
msgstr ""
"ほら、マップに印を付けておこう。気軽に立ち寄ってくれ。物資の交換に来てもいいし、もし腕に自信があるなら、傭兵として雇うこともあるかもしれない。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hey, thanks.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "どうも、助かるよ。では、物資の取り引きをしよう。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hi again.  You want something?"
msgstr "また会ったな。何か用？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "How do I get there?"
msgstr "どこにあるんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I can understand that.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "それもそうか。では、物資の取り引きをしよう。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I won't try anything if you don't.  Just passing through."
msgstr "通りがかっただけだ。そちらが何もしてこないなら、手は出さないよ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm a caravan guard, working for the Free Merchants.  I'm an independent "
"contractor though.  Seems like a good way to get safety in numbers and try "
"to find a safe place to settle down."
msgstr "私は隊商の護衛として、自由商人のもとで働いている。とは言っても、単なる個人契約だが。人も多いし、安全を確保するのに丁度いいと思ってな。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm good for the moment, but you can usually find a merc or two waiting "
"between jobs, back at the Free Merchant base."
msgstr "今のところは間に合ってるよ。自由商人の拠点へ行けば、暇な傭兵の一人や二人いるだろう。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "It's a living, eh?  I'd better get going."
msgstr "なるほど、そうやって暮らしているのか。そろそろ行かないと。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers "
"directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "申し訳ないが、見ず知らずの者に隠れ家の場所を教えたりしたら、お客にそっぽを向かれてしまうよ。自分の足で探してくれ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
